Key empirical findings include:
\begin{itemize}
    \item \textbf{Dual-Metric Faithfulness Leadership:} Distinguishing overall faithfulness (awarding perfect scores to epistemic refusals) from answer-only faithfulness (evaluating generated legal arguments) is critical. TERRA attains the highest overall faithfulness ($\TerraOverallFaithfulnessMean$, 95\% CI $\TerraOverallCI$) ahead of HippoRAG-Adapted ($\HippoRAGOverallFaithfulnessMean$, $\HippoRAGOverallCI$), whose confidence intervals overlap, and the highest answer-only faithfulness ($\TerraAnswerOnlyFaithfulnessMean$ vs.\ $\HippoRAGAnswerOnlyFaithfulnessMean$ for HippoRAG); answer-only scores are conditional on different answered subsets (TERRA answers $\TerraAnsweredQueries$/350 queries, HippoRAG \HippoRAGAnswerOnlyCount, Flat \FlatRAGAnswerOnlyCount, GraphRAG \GraphRAGAnswerOnlyCount). Flagged refusals total $\TerraFlaggedRefusals$/350 for TERRA against $\HippoRAGFlaggedRefusals$ for HippoRAG, $\FlatRAGFlaggedRefusals$ for Flat and $\GraphRAGFlaggedRefusals$ for GraphRAG ($\TerraEpistemicRefusals$, $\HippoEpistemicRefusals$, $\FlatEpistemicRefusals$ and $\GraphEpistemicRefusals$ counting unflagged textual refusals).
    \item \textbf{Evolutionary Multi-Hop Performance (Category B):} On multi-decade precedent trajectories, TERRA achieves $\TerraCatBFaithfulness$ faithfulness, significantly outperforming all evaluated retrieval baselines: HippoRAG ($\HippoRAGCatBFaithfulness$, $\Delta=\CatBTerraVsHippoRAGDelta$, $q=\CatBTerraVsHippoRAGAdjQ$), GraphRAG ($\GraphRAGCatBFaithfulness$, $\Delta=\CatBTerraVsGraphRAGDelta$, $q=\CatBTerraVsGraphRAGAdjQ$), and Flat Vector RAG ($\FlatRAGCatBFaithfulness$, $\Delta=\CatBTerraVsFlatDelta$, $q=\CatBTerraVsFlatRAGAdjQ$). A non-retrieval Direct LLM scores higher on Category~B ($\DirectLLMCatBFaithfulness$, $\Delta=\CatBTerraVsDirectLLMDelta$, $q=\CatBTerraVsDirectLLMAdjQ$; TERRA win rate $\TerraVsDirectLLMCatBWinRate$), consistent with dual judges rewarding fluent ungrounded parametric prose over grounded retrieval constraints, whereas TERRA's retrieval evaluation shows stronger Category~B citation coverage and full-precedent-path recovery.
    \item \textbf{Factual Lookup Performance (Category A):} On Category~A, TERRA scores $\TerraCatAFaithfulness$ against HippoRAG $\HippoRAGCatAFaithfulness$, Flat $\FlatRAGCatAFaithfulness$ and Direct LLM $\DirectLLMCatAFaithfulness$; it is significantly higher than Direct ($\CatATerraVsDirectLLMDelta$) and Flat ($\CatATerraVsFlatRAGDelta$, $q=\CatATerraVsFlatRAGAdjQ$) and statistically indistinguishable from GraphRAG ($\CatATerraVsGraphRAGDelta$, $q=\CatATerraVsGraphRAGAdjQ$) and HippoRAG ($\CatATerraVsHippoRAGDelta$, $q=\CatATerraVsHippoRAGAdjQ$). The safety gate falsely refuses $\TerraCatAFalseRefusals$/100 Category~A queries (and $\TerraCatBFalseRefusals$/100 on Category~B; see Limitation~\ref{item:falserefusal}).
